One context written two ways gets one class and one rule text: the rule
prints the canonical form that the class hashes (sorted pseudo-classes,
lowercase pseudo-class names and media feature names). Two files that use
the two spellings build one rule, in either order.

  $ cat > a.ml <<EOF
  > let a = [%css "&:hover:focus { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > b.ml <<EOF
  > let b = [%css "&:focus:hover { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > c.ml <<EOF
  > let c = [%css "&:HOVER { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > d.ml <<EOF
  > let d = [%css "&:hover { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > e.ml <<EOF
  > let e = [%css "@media (MIN-WIDTH: 1px) { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > f.ml <<EOF
  > let f = [%css "@media (min-width: 1px) { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ for m in a b c d e f; do ../../standalone.exe --env production --impl $m.ml -o out_$m.ml; done

  $ styled-ppx.generate out_a.ml out_b.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._c7f-QfSkE1JM33Y:focus:hover{color:red;}
  $ styled-ppx.generate out_b.ml out_a.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._c7f-QfSkE1JM33Y:focus:hover{color:red;}
  $ styled-ppx.generate out_c.ml out_d.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._c7f1Tl5-wvpMs6j:hover{color:red;}
  $ styled-ppx.generate out_d.ml out_c.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._c7f1Tl5-wvpMs6j:hover{color:red;}
  $ styled-ppx.generate out_e.ml out_f.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @media (min-width:1px){._c7f-T3I8pU4gQ5t{color:red;}}
  $ styled-ppx.generate out_f.ml out_e.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @media (min-width:1px){._c7f-T3I8pU4gQ5t{color:red;}}

Whitespace inside a condition does not change the context: the class and
the printed prelude use one canonical form. Spaces stay between words and
before a `(` that follows a word; quoted strings stay as written.

  $ cat > g.ml <<EOF
  > let g = [%css "@media (min-width:1px) { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > h.ml <<EOF
  > let h = [%css "@media screen and (min-width:1px) { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > i.ml <<EOF
  > let i = [%css "@media screen   and (  min-width : 1px  ) { color: red; }"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > j.ml <<EOF
  > let j = [%css {|@supports (content: "a  b") { color: red; }|}]
  > EOF
  $ cat > k.ml <<EOF
  > let k = [%css {|@supports (content:"a  b") { color: red; }|}]
  > EOF
  $ cat > l.ml <<EOF
  > let l = [%css {|@supports (content: "a b") { color: red; }|}]
  > EOF
  $ for m in g h i j k l; do ../../standalone.exe --env production --impl $m.ml -o out_$m.ml; done

